SCOPE AND EXCLUSIONS (layered licensing)

This MIT grant covers the portfolio's source code, build scripts, tests and
documentation authored by the owner. It does NOT cover, and grants no rights
in:

- `public/images` and every image file anywhere under `public/` (employer /
  workplace logos, project imagery, social link icons, photos). These are
  owner-confirmed workplace or owner-authored assets retained for the owner's
  employment history; see `ASSETS.md` for per-file provenance. They remain the
  property of their respective owners and are NOT relicensed under MIT.
- Site content and post copy under `src/content/` (including blog text,
  disclosed metrics and named individuals). Provenance/permissions are
  recorded in `ASSETS.md`; the owner has confirmed NDA and consent gates.
- Fonts (the vendored Anton woff2 and its SIL Open Font License text in
  `public/fonts/ANTON-OFL.txt`). Fonts are governed by the OFL, not MIT.
- Third-party dependencies. Their notices and licenses are listed in
  `LICENSES.md` and in each package's own distribution.

`ASSETS.md` is provenance evidence, not a license grant.
